  "narrative": "The H49 validation confirms the high-feature_043 subgroup result for feature_065 on outcome_013. The signed discovery effect was +0.0975 with interval +0.0281 to +0.1669, and the independent validation effect was +0.1163 with adjusted interval +0.0326 to +0.2000. Using the approximate absolute-mean clinical scale for outcome_013, the 10% threshold is about +0.0269, so the validation lower bound itself exceeds the clinically meaningful threshold and is positive. I therefore keep H49 as an accepted dataset-specific association and close this particular subgroup investigation because it is now both replicated and clinically supported. The H26 response deadline is resolved by validation: the feature_060-by-high-feature_043 interaction on outcome_006 had a nonclinical discovery interval and the validation estimate was near zero with an interval spanning zero and the opposite sign. I keep H26 rejected and closed, so the broader feature_060 interaction pathway on outcome_006 is deprioritized. The strongest conclusion in this dataset remains that feature_065=1 is associated with stronger outcome_013 dependency relative to feature_065=0, including across feature_060 strata and both high and low feature_043 strata. This supports outcome-013-specific robustness rather than a broad dependency-modifier effect. The most informative next work is to complete the outcome-specificity panel for feature_065 and to test formally whether feature_043 modifies the feature_065 association, while also keeping the near-threshold reversed feature_063 result on outcome_014 and the pending categorical stratum claims under observation. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset and are not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current evidence state: Feature_065 is the central supported predictor and is dataset-specific, not generalized. H35 main feature_065=1 versus 0 on outcome_013 remains accepted and independently validated: discovery +0.1169 [0.0823,0.1516], validation +0.1319 [0.0801,0.1838]; approximate outcome_013 10% threshold ~0.0269. Robust subgroup acceptance: H45 feature_060=1 +0.1370 [0.0881,0.1860]; H46 feature_060=0 +0.0969 [0.0476,0.1462]; H50 low feature_043 +0.1247 [0.0847,0.1646]; H49 high feature_043 discovery +0.0975 [0.0281,0.1669], validation +0.1163 [0.0326,0.2000], now accepted and closed. H47 feature_060 interaction +0.0401 [-0.0292,0.1094] unresolved/closed: no reliable modification by feature_060. H53 feature_008=0 +0.1150 [0.0145,0.2155] unresolved/deferred because small n and lower below threshold. Outcome specificity: feature_065 is rejected for stronger outcome_008 and outcome_011 dependency, null/closed for outcome_006, imprecise/unresolved for outcome_001 and outcome_012, and unresolved active for outcome_014 overall with near-threshold but zero-crossing interval. H26 interaction feature_060-high-feature_043 on outcome_006 is rejected/closed after validation; discovery +0.0601 [-0.0148,0.1351], validation -0.0049 [-0.1134,0.1035], outcome_006 threshold ~0.0093. Feature_063 near-threshold candidate: H43 reversed level_002 versus level_001 on outcome_014 is +0.0361 [0.0022,0.0701], active but not accepted because lower bound is below approximate threshold ~0.0093; H48 level_003 versus level_001 outcome_014 is small-n and deferred; H55 pending high-feature_043 feature_063 test. Other active/pending claims: H44 feature_065 in feature_008=1, H51/H52 feature_061 median splits, H55 feature_063 high-feature_043, H60 feature_048 categorical, H13 feature_002 in feature_008=1/high-feature_043 outcome_010, H30 feature_036 outcome_014. Next registered analyses: complete feature_065 outcome panel for outcome_005, outcome_015, outcome_002, outcome_007, outcome_004, outcome_009, outcome_010, and outcome_003 in the stronger-dependency direction, plus a formal feature_043 interaction test for the accepted feature_065 outcome_013 association. All statements remain dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or generalized claims."
